All,

Note that 2G and 3G refer to different "Product Design Platforms" from whic=
h the different Philmac Product Lines are derived;  IPS-OD, IPS-ID, CTS, an=
d Kitec/XPA/QLine.

IPS-OD Philmac fitting configurations in 2" diameter will now only be shipp=
ed in 2G form.  The 2" 3G form is no longer available for sale.

This will simplify communication of the installation procedure for the 2" s=
ize to just one procedure, that of the 2G form.

The 3" IPS-OD fittings are of the 2G form.

All other sizes and configurations in IPS-OD, IPS-ID, CTS, and Kitec/XPA/QL=
ine Philmac product lines are of the 3G form.

Some 2" configurations previously available in 3G form will not be availabl=
e in 2G form for the time being.  These are historically low unit volume it=
ems.  There may be some customers that question the absence of the low volu=
me 2" configurations.   Advise the customer that with the upgrade some conf=
igurations will lag and possibly not be included if sufficient demand is no=
t present.  Please advise me of the details of such enquiries by purpose wr=
itten email so that we might gage demand and advise Philmac of the need for=
 additions.  Identify the configuration, quantity, name, company name, and =
phone number.

The IPS-OD Philmac price sheet will be updated shortly to reflect those 2" =
configurations that have been removed.  Guidance on deployment of the new p=
rice sheets will follow.

Some 2" 3G inventory remains that will be disposed of.  It is not available=
 for sale.  There will be no exceptions.

A decision will be made shortly about part numbers for the 2" diameters whi=
ch have used either a "75-" or "77-" part number prefix depending on whethe=
r the form was 3G or 2G respectively.  You will be advised accordingly.

j



